ryContext.recordScene", "op": "create", "path": "Berreman/OpticalConstructor/OpticalConstructor.Storage/KitContentFiles.fs", "obligations": ["S43-RECORD"]}], "packages": [], "checks": []}

**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** A kit's experiment and scene files are recorded with the library versions they reference (001 §E 'Library closure snapshot: every library version the kit references is copied into library/ when first referenced'; 001 §C 'A version becomes Pinned … when a kit first references it'; step 139: `snapshotReferences`' callers are the writers of kit content that binds library versions). In `KitContentFiles.fs`, on a `type KitLibraryContext with` extension (step 139), each member documented in one to three lines citing spec 0050 S4.3: (1) `member this.recordExperiment (experiment : Experiment) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` calls `this.snapshotReferences experiment.libraryReferences` (steps 137, 139), then `this.kit.proxy.writeExperiment experiment` (step 148), a `KitError` wrapped as `KitLibraryKitErr`. The snapshots come first, so a written file never references a version the kit lacks; on a failure the file is not written and what the snapshot wrote stays (step 139). (2) `member this.recordScene (name : SceneName) (scene : SceneSnapshot) : Result<unit, KitLibraryError>` does the same with `scene.libraryReferences` (step 147) and `writeScene` (step 148). Removing an experiment snapshots nothing and keeps the kit's snapshots, which other files may reference: it calls `deleteExperiment` directly (step 152). No other member is added. Tests, new facts in `KitLibraryTests` (step 139), over its Built-in library, its recorder of pins and its in-memory kit opened read-write. `recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file`: an experiment whose setup binds the multilayer sample (`SampleIds.multilayerQwId`) at version 1 and the 600 nm source preset by its entry id, recorded through `recordExperiment`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the sample, its materials, their categories and the source preset, each once; the recorder holds every one of those versions; and `kit.proxy.readExperiments ()` answers the experiment. `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind`: a scene whose elements bind the 600 nm source preset and the multilayer sample by value id, beside one unbound detector, recorded through `recordScene` under `Bench`, leaves `listSnapshots` holding the source, the multilayer at its latest version, its materials and their categories, and `readScene` answers the scene. `a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing`: an experiment binding a test-local GUID by entry id answers `UnheldEntryErr` naming it, `readExperiments` answers `[]`, and `paths` is unchanged. `a read-only kit records nothing`: over a context opened with `ReadOnlyKitAccess`, `recordExperiment` answers `KitLibraryKitErr (KitReadOnlyErr _)`, the recorder is empty and `paths` is unchanged.

**Acceptance.** After the recording members land, `KitLibraryContext.recordExperiment` and `recordScene` MUST snapshot every library version the file references, pinning it, before they write the file, and write nothing when a reference cannot be resolved; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `recording an experiment snapshots the library versions it binds, then writes its file`, `recording a scene snapshots the entries its elements bind`, `a reference the library and the kit cannot resolve records nothing`, `a read-only kit records nothing`, the count rising by 4; and build, elevation and the eleven s17 invariants MUST pass.
